<title>USA: Dominick's Supermarkets to challenge suit.</title>
<headline>Dominick's Supermarkets to challenge suit.</headline>
<dateline>NORTHLAKE, Ill. 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dominick's Supermarkets Inc said it will vigorously defend itself against a class-action lawsuit that a judge on Tuesday ruled may proceed.</p>
<p>The supermarket chain is accused of discriminating against female employees in a class-action suit originally filed in March of 1995, when Dominick's was privately held. The company allegedly failed to provide promotional opportunities, work experience and training to the women as it allegedly provided to its male workers.</p>
<p>Dominick's operates about 100 grocery stores.</p>
<p>Its shares were off 3/8 Wednesday at 22-1/4.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
